</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">no openssl or wolfssl are used as client in order to=
 check interoperability with tls-se server<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">tls-se is of course a specific impl=C3=A9mentation f=
or tls13 server in javacard..it is written in java but an =C3=B4ter impl=C3=
=A9mentation is written in c for constraint notes. as written in
 the draft tls-se implementation has three software blocks: crypto lib, tls=
 state machine, and tls lib<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
</div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
<div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Le lun. 21 sept. 2020 =C3=A0 14:36, Hannes Tschofeni=
g &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.com" target=3D"_blank">Hannes=
.Tschofenig@arm.com</a>&gt; a =C3=A9crit=C2=A0:<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<blockquote style=3D"border-top:none;border-right:none;border-bottom:none;b=
order-left:1pt solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0in 0in 0in 6pt;margin:5pt 0i=
n 5pt 4.8pt">
<div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Hi Pascal,
<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">are you saying that the stack on the secure element =
uses WolfSSL or OpenSSL? I am sure that WolfSSL works well but for code siz=
e reasons I doubt OpenSSL is possible. Can you confirm?
<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">In case of WolfSSL, you have multiple options for cr=
edentials, including plain PSK, PSK-ECDHE, raw public keys, and certificate=
s as I noted in my mail to the UTA list:
<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><a href=3D"https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/uta=
/RJ4wU77D6f7qslfwrc16jkrPTew/" target=3D"_blank">https://mailarchive.ietf.o=
rg/arch/msg/uta/RJ4wU77D6f7qslfwrc16jkrPTew/</a><u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Ciao<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Hannes<u></u><u></u></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
<div style=3D"border-right:none;border-bottom:none;border-left:none;border-=
top:1pt solid rgb(225,225,225);padding:3pt 0in 0in">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><b>From:</b> Pascal Urien &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:pasc=
al.urien@gmail.com" target=3D"_blank">pascal.urien@gmail.com</a>&gt;
<br>
<b>Sent:</b> Monday, September 21, 2020 2:01 PM<br>
<b>To:</b> Hannes Tschofenig &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.co=
m" target=3D"_blank">Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.com</a>&gt;<br>
<b>Cc:</b> Filippo Valsorda &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:filippo@ml.filippo.io" ta=
rget=3D"_blank">filippo@ml.filippo.io</a>&gt;;
<a href=3D"mailto:tls@ietf.org" target=3D"_blank">tls@ietf.org</a><br>
<b>Subject:</b> Re: [TLS] The future of external PSK in TLS 1.3<u></u><u></=
u></p>
</div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Hi Hannes<u></u><u></u></p>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Yes it has been tested with several=C2=A0 3.04 Javac=
ards=C2=A0 commercially available<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">In the draft
<a href=3D"https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-urien-tls-se-00" target=3D"_bl=
ank">https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-urien-tls-se-00</a>=C2=A0 =C2=A0Sect=
ion 5-ISO 7816 Use Case, the exchanges are done with the existing implement=
ation<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">TLS-SE TLS1.3 PSK+ECDH server works with ESP8266 or =
Arduino+Ethernet boards=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">For client software=C2=A0we use OPENSSL or WolfSSL<u=
></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Pascal<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
</div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">=C2=A0<u></u><u></u></p>
<div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Le=C2=A0lun. 21 sept. 2020 =C3=A0=C2=A012:35, Hannes=
 Tschofenig &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.com" target=3D"_bla=
nk">Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.com</a>&gt; a =C3=A9crit=C2=A0:<u></u><u></u></p>
</div>
<blockquote style=3D"border-top:none;border-right:none;border-bottom:none;b=
order-left:1pt solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0in 0in 0in 6pt;margin:5pt 0i=
n 5pt 4.8pt">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Hi Pascal,<br>
<br>
Thanks for the pointer to the draft.<br>
<br>
Since I am surveying implementations for the update of RFC 7925 (see <a hre=
f=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-uta-tls13-iot-profile/" ta=
rget=3D"_blank">
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-uta-tls13-iot-profile/</a>) I w=
as wondering whether there is an implementation of this approach.<br>
<br>
Ciao<br>
Hannes<br>
<br>
<br>
From: Pascal Urien &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:pascal.urien@gmail.com" target=3D"=
_blank">pascal.urien@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>
Sent: Monday, September 21, 2020 11:44 AM<br>
To: Hannes Tschofenig &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.com" targ=
et=3D"_blank">Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.com</a>&gt;<br>
Cc: Filippo Valsorda &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:filippo@ml.filippo.io" target=3D=
"_blank">filippo@ml.filippo.io</a>&gt;;
<a href=3D"mailto:tls@ietf.org" target=3D"_blank">tls@ietf.org</a><br>
Subject: Re: [TLS] The future of external PSK in TLS 1.3<br>
<br>
Hi All<br>
<br>
Here is an example of PSK+ECDHE for IoT<br>
<br>
<a href=3D"https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-urien-tls-se-00" target=3D"_bl=
ank">https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-urien-tls-se-00</a>=C2=A0 uses TLS1.=
3 server=C2=A0 PSK+ECDHE for secure elements<br>
<br>
The security level in these devices is as high as EAL5+<br>
<br>
The computing time is about 1.4s for a PSK+ECDHE session (AES-128-CCM, + se=
cp256r1)<br>
<br>
The real critical resource is the required RAM size, less than 1KB in our e=
xperiments<br>
<br>
The secure element=C2=A0 only needs a classical TCP/IP interface (i.e. sock=
ets like)<br>
<br>
Trusted PSK should avoid selfie attacks<br>
<br>
Pascal<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
Le lun. 21 sept. 2020 =C3=A0 11:29, Hannes Tschofenig &lt;mailto:<a href=3D=
"mailto:Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.com" target=3D"_blank">Hannes.Tschofenig@arm.=
com</a>&gt; a =C3=A9crit :<br>
Hi Filippo,<br>
<br>
=E2=80=A2 Indeed, if the SCADA industry has a particular need, they should =
profile TLS for use in that industry, and not require we change the recomme=
ndation for the open Internet.<br>
<br>
We have an IoT profile for TLS and it talks about the use of PSK, see <a hr=
ef=3D"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7925" target=3D"_blank">
https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7925</a><br>
<br>
On the =E2=80=9Copen Internet=E2=80=9D (probably referring to the Web usage=
) you are not going to use PSKs in TLS. There is a separate RFC that provid=
es recommendations for that environmnent, see RFC 752. That RFC is currentl=
y being revised, see
<a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-sheffer-uta-rfc7525bis/" =
target=3D"_blank">
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-sheffer-uta-rfc7525bis/</a><br>
<br>
Ciao<br>
Hannes<br>
